<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>Is China the cheapest source for every battery?</h3>
<p>No. China is usually the lowest-cost source at scale, but freight, tariffs and certification can erase the advantage for small or regulated orders. Compare landed cost, not ex-works price.</p>
<h3>Why are India and Southeast Asia growing?</h3>
<p>Localisation policy, two-wheeler electrification and storage demand are pulling assembly and cell capacity into those markets. The growth is real but uneven; check the country page for the segment that applies to your product.</p>
